<tr><td><strong>First important use</strong></td><td>Define and check Morphir’s own IR and SDK, then replace covered JSON Schema gates.</td></tr></tbody></table><p><strong>Review route:</strong> <a href="#decisions">decisions</a> → <a href="#language">syntax</a> → <a href="#self-specification">dogfooding</a> → <a href="#acceptance">acceptance</a>.</p>
<details data-reference="intent-0"><summary>Full intent and agreed outcomes</summary>
<p>Morphir should carry an idea from initial prose through requirements, domain concepts, contracts and implementations, retaining why each part exists. A person can begin with a paragraph, use a PRD to organize requirements, adopt EARS where useful, and progressively make selected rules executable. Functional, non-functional, data and other requirements can coexist at different degrees of formalization.</p>
<p>The maintainer wants a Morphir-specific DSL/IDL with functional modules, types and operations; type refinements, invariants, preconditions and postconditions; extensible linked metadata; and the ability to make and analyze claims about intent. Generating tests, Gherkin and potentially EARS is an explicit outcome. Early delivery belongs in morphir-moonbit, with shared specifications, KB content and documentation added incrementally to finos/morphir.</p>
<p><strong>Maintainer clarification:</strong> type definitions must favor an ML-family functional style. F#, OCaml, Elm and Gleam are non-exhaustive sources of inspiration. The language should express algebraic data types, records, aliases, type parameters and function types naturally within Morphir modules. Choosing one existing language's exact grammar is still open.</p>
<p><strong>Maintainer clarification:</strong> provide opaque type aliases for newtypes. Restore Elm-style <code>type alias</code> for transparent aliases and records, and <code>opaque type alias</code> for newtypes. Use <code>type</code> for algebraic declarations. Accept a leading pipe before the first constructor, but do not require it. This supersedes draft 0.4's proposed unified declarations and mandatory leading pipe. Generics and type variables are required core capabilities, including parameterized declarations and polymorphic signatures.</p>
<p>The example portfolio includes Kanban, Go Fish, blackjack, canonical rentals extended toward securities lending, GAAP accounting and a bounded SCRA example. The previously asked Kanban full-column question remains deferred. No specific Kanban policy has been selected.</p>
<p><strong>Maintainer priority:</strong> define the Morphir IR and Morphir SDK themselves as Morphir specifications, and use Morphir tools to check implementations against those specifications. Land this dogfooding early. Replace JSON Schema as the definition/checking dependency in the compatibility kit and verification scenarios. The migration must cover its existing obligations before removing the corresponding gate.</p>
<p><strong>Maintainer clarification:</strong> tuple support must extend beyond pairs, with no fixed small-arity ceiling. This applies to the core declaration and execution capabilities, including generic tuple elements.</p>
<p><strong>Maintainer clarification:</strong> include untagged unions of existing types alongside constructor-based algebraic types. Add a first-class untagged union type expression to the Morphir IR 4.0.0 draft as well; this is a core type-system capability, not merely descriptive metadata.</p>
<p><strong>Maintainer decision:</strong> begin function specifications with plain <code>fn</code> declarations and named, typed parameters. The intended direction is a full Morphir language with a first-class frontend and backend that map the supported Morphir features completely. Keep <code>declare</code>, separate file extensions and other specification/implementation markers as future options; none is selected now. This direction does not add a general implementation language to the first preview.</p>
<p>Success is a small model that remains useful before implementation: a user can inspect its requirements, evaluate supported rules against examples, generate readable scenarios, and later check an implementation without losing the original intent. The broader domain portfolio guides the model; completing every domain is not a prerequisite for the first preview.</p>
</details>
</section>

