<main>
<h1>Reduce redundant CI work while preserving platform and release coverage</h1>
<p class="meta">morphir-ukvn.5.65 · 17 October 2026 · Proposed epic</p>
<nav class="toc" aria-label="Contents"><ul><li><a href="#problem-statement">Problem statement</a></li><li><a href="#outcome">Outcome</a></li><li><a href="#high-level-proposed-solutions">High-level proposed solutions</a></li><li><a href="#delivery-approach">Delivery approach</a></li><li><a href="#acceptance-criteria">Acceptance criteria</a></li><li><a href="#scope-and-non-goals">Scope and non-goals</a></li><li><a href="#related-work">Related work</a></li></ul></nav>
<section id="problem-statement"><h2>Problem statement</h2>
<p>CI in finos/morphir-moonbit repeats static validation, dependency setup and builds, and selects expensive qualification more broadly than the changed components require. Contributors wait longer for useful feedback and the project consumes unnecessary runner time, including macOS capacity.</p>
<p>In successful run 39065090591 on 17 October 2026, checks spanned approximately 23 minutes from the first job starting to ci-ok completing. Installed lifecycle took about 13 minutes on Linux and 17 minutes on macOS; signed-provider acceptance took about 13 and 14 minutes respectively. These are single-run elapsed job durations, not billed minutes or a representative statistical baseline. The repeated TypeScript checks took 12 seconds on Linux, 17 seconds on macOS and 45 seconds on Windows. The long qualification jobs, repeated prerequisites and broad selection therefore deserve attention beyond removing the TypeScript OS matrix.</p>
<p>Evidence: <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/actions/runs/39065090591">https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/actions/runs/39065090591</a></p>
</section>
<section id="outcome"><h2>Outcome</h2>
<p>Reduce CI runner consumption and time to actionable feedback while preserving platform-specific behavior checks, supported compiler/backend coverage, exact-candidate release qualification and fail-closed aggregate gates.</p>
</section>
<section id="high-level-proposed-solutions"><h2>High-level proposed solutions</h2>
<ol><li>Establish a measured baseline. Record queue time, execution time, critical path, job/OS runner minutes, setup/build/test breakdowns and cache hits for comparable focused and full runs. Separate observed duration from billing and normalize comparisons for workload and cache state.</li><li>Remove redundant static work. Finish the Linux-only TypeScript change tracked by morphir-ukvn.5.63. Run YAML lint once rather than in both Lint and Validate Configuration Files. Keep checked-build rejection tests and package validation. Changing legacy task wrappers must follow the repository&#x27;s MoonBit migration policy.</li><li>Separate dependency setup from runtime compilation. Let static-only jobs install pinned tooling and frozen dependencies without emitting runtime JavaScript. Keep runtime builds in jobs that consume those files; evaluate same-run reuse where useful.</li><li>Refine component dependency selection. Extend scripts/ci-changes.mbtx so isolated changes avoid unrelated embedding/browser, Elm/Scheme, site and acceptance work. Test direct and transitive dependencies, renames, shared inputs and unknown paths. Unknown or ambiguous changes continue to select conservative coverage.</li><li>Refine full-qualification triggers. Distinguish workflow wiring changes from compiler, dependency, platform-setup and shared CI-policy changes. Workflow changes must exercise the workflows and gates they affect; toolchain and policy changes retain full qualification until a tested narrower mapping proves equivalent. Preserve scheduled full qualification and qualification of the exact release candidate.</li><li>Cache reproducible dependency downloads. Evaluate Bun package downloads, Mooncakes registry/packages and other measured setup costs. Key caches by relevant OS/architecture, toolchain and lockfile/dependency identities. A cache miss or stale cache must remain safe. Do not cache trust decisions, signing state, acceptance receipts or mutable fixture state.</li><li>Reuse compatible build outputs. Audit repeated JavaScript/native compilation and extend existing same-run artifact producers where they reduce measured cost. Consumers must verify source, target, compiler and dependency identity. Keep independent backend, fresh-installation and debug/release checks where they cover distinct behavior.</li></ol>
</section>
<section id="delivery-approach"><h2>Delivery approach</h2>
<p>Start with measurement and duplicate static/setup work, then improve selection rules, then introduce caches and artifact reuse only where the measurements support them. Deliver reviewable slices with before/after evidence and an explicit coverage comparison. This epic is a proposal for implementation; it does not authorize removing acceptance criteria or bypassing required checks.</p>
</section>
<section id="acceptance-criteria"><h2>Acceptance criteria</h2>
<ul><li>Baseline and after-change measurements are recorded for comparable focused and full workflows, with queue time and execution time distinguished. Target reductions are selected from that baseline rather than invented in advance.</li><li>TypeScript static checking runs once; runtime OS matrices and Wasm, Wasm GC, JavaScript and native behavior coverage remain where required.</li><li>YAML lint and other identified static checks run once per relevant workflow path; static-only jobs avoid unnecessary runtime compilation.</li><li>Selection changes have positive and negative tests, including transitive/shared dependencies and conservative unknown-path behavior. Selected failures or cancellations cannot produce a green aggregate gate.</li><li>Scheduled full qualification and exact-candidate release qualification remain available and required at the appropriate boundaries.</li><li>Cache misses and invalid artifacts exercise safe fallbacks; stale, incompatible or untrusted state cannot satisfy qualification.</li><li>Each optimization records its retained coverage and measured impact. Material regressions have a documented rollback path.</li></ul>
</section>
<section id="scope-and-non-goals"><h2>Scope and non-goals</h2>
<p>Scope: .github/workflows/, .github/actions/, scripts/ci-changes.mbtx, scripts/ci-gate.mbtx, related portable task scripts and CI documentation. Do not remove process-supervision OS matrices, collapse distinct MoonBit backend behavior tests, weaken signed-provider/artifact admission, change release policy or alter repository protection settings as an incidental optimization. Cost estimates and percentage reduction targets remain open until baseline data is collected.</p>
</section>
<section id="related-work"><h2>Related work</h2>
<ul><li>morphir-ukvn.5.63: Linux-only static TypeScript checks; implemented locally but not yet landed at the time this epic was written.</li><li>morphir-ukvn.5.61 / PR #129: complete pinned Unix MoonBit setup, including Linux ARM64; preserve its fresh-install platform checks when setup changes.</li><li>morphir-ukvn.5.59: migration of legacy mise automation to portable MoonBit scripts.</li></ul>
</section>
</main>
</body>
</html>

