- Produces (private to the worker package):
  - `priv struct ProjectFile { path : @ids.SourcePath; content : String }` — `path` is relative to the project root, for example `src/Workbench/Main.elm` or `morphir.json`.
  - `priv struct ProjectRequest { name : @ids.SourcePackageName; language : @ids.LanguageId; provider : @ids.ProviderId?; profile : @ids.ProfileId?; files : Array[ProjectFile]; exposed : Array[@ids.SourceModuleName] }`
  - `fn project_request(request : Json, offers : Array[@engine.LanguageOffer]) -> ProjectRequest raise`
    - With a `project` object: reads `name`, `languageId`, `frontendProvider?`, `frontendProfile?`, `exposedModules?` and `files[]` (`{path, content}`) from it.
    - Without one (the `source` shorthand): reads `languageId` (default `scheme`), `frontendProvider?`, `frontendProfile?` and `source` from the request. Elm: the module header gives the path `src/<A>/<B>/<C>.elm`, the package `A.B` and the exposed module `C`. Other languages: one file `src/main<first extension of the offer>`, package `user`.
    - Raises `@wire.Invalid("workbench.unavailable_language", "This local input language is unavailable: <id>")` for a language that no offer has.
  - `fn elm_module_name(source : String) -> String?`
  - `fn project_tree(project : ProjectRequest) -> @workspace.Tree` — adds `morphir.toml` from `manifest` when the project has neither `morphir.json` nor `morphir.toml`; `directories` holds `""` and every parent directory of every file.
  - `fn manifest(project : ProjectRequest) -> String`
  - `fn overlay(project : ProjectRequest, backend : String) -> @config.Document raise`
  - `fn toml_string(text : String) -> String` — a TOML basic string with `\` and `"` escaped.

