### Task 1: Value definitions, names, lambdas and patterns

Introduce value lowering: one top-level value becomes an `ExpressionBody` with morphir-elm's argument lift. This task lowers names, lambdas, parentheses, unit and every pattern; Tasks 2 and 3 add the other expression kinds.

**Files:**
- Create: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/lower/values.mbt` (the `Lowering` state, `lower_value_definition`, `value_attributes`, expression dispatch)
- Create: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/lower/patterns.mbt`
- Create: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/lower/show_test.mbt` (a test-only text form of values and patterns)
- Create: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/lower/values_test.mbt`
- Modify: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/lower/signatures.mbt` (move `placeholder`, `function_parts` where `values.mbt` can use them; keep `lower_value_signature` until Task 4)

**Interfaces:**
- Consumes: `@resolve.Scope::resolve_value(Array[String], String, (String) -> Bool) -> Resolved raise ResolveError`, `Resolved { Local(String); Global(FQName); BoolLiteral(Bool) }`; `lower_type(scope, node, None)`; `@mapping.elm_name`.
- Produces (package `finos/morphir-elm/frontend/lower`):
  - `pub fn value_attributes(@ast.Range) -> @ir.ValueAttributes` — default attributes with `source: Some(location)`.
  - `pub fn lower_value_definition(@resolve.Scope, @ast.Function) -> (String, @ir.ValueDefinition) raise LowerError` — (Elm name, `ExpressionBody(inputs, output, body)`).
  - Private: `priv struct Lowering { scope, locals : Array[Map[String, Bool]], placeholders : Ref[Int] }` with `expression(Self, @ast.Node[@ast.Expression]) -> @ir.Value raise LowerError` and `pattern(Self, @ast.Node[@ast.Pattern], Map[String, Bool]) -> @ir.Pattern raise LowerError` (the map collects the names the pattern binds). Placeholders are numbered per declaration from 0 (`t-0`, `t-1`, …) and carry the unknown marker.

Rules (confirmed facts 3, 6, 7, 10):
- `FunctionOrValue(q, n)`: `resolve_value(q, n, is_local)`; `Local` → `Variable(elm_name(n))`; `BoolLiteral(b)` → `Literal(BoolLiteral(b))`; `Global(fq)` → `Constructor` when `n` starts upper case, else `Reference`. A `ResolveError(code, message)` is `LowerError(code, message, Some(range))`.
- `ParenthesizedExpression(e)` → `e`. `UnitExpr` → `Unit`. `LambdaExpression` → one frame with every name its argument patterns bind, then `Lambda(pattern, …)` per argument, innermost last.
- Every other expression kind raises `LowerError("elm.unsupported", "<kind> is not lowered yet", Some(range))`; Tasks 2 and 3 replace each of these arms.
- Patterns: confirmed fact 6. `NamedPattern({module_name, name}, args)`: unqualified `True`/`False` → `LiteralPattern(BoolLiteral)`; otherwise resolve the constructor with `resolve_value(qualifier, name, _ => false)` (a constructor is never local) and lower the arguments. `IntPattern(n)`/`HexPattern(n)` → `IntegerLiteral(n.to_string())`. `FloatPattern(d)` → `FloatLiteral(d)`. `RecordPattern` → `LowerError("elm.unsupported", "a record pattern is not supported", Some(range))`.
- `lower_value_definition`: collect the declaration arguments, then the arguments of each leading lambda of the body (looking through `ParenthesizedExpression`), into one list, and the body after them. Bind every name the list binds in one frame. Lift from the front while the pattern is `VarPattern` and the rest of the annotation, looking through a single-item `Tupled`, is a `FunctionTypeAnnotation` (unannotated: lift every leading `VarPattern`, each input a fresh placeholder). The output is the rest of the annotation, or a fresh placeholder. Wrap the remaining arguments around the lowered body as `Lambda` nodes. Every node gets `value_attributes(range)` of its syntax node.

