### Task 3: Name resolution

Build the project symbol table and resolve every type, value, constructor and operator name to an FQName or a local. Also compute the project modules that a declaration references, which Task 6 uses for module selection.

**Files:**
- Create: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/resolve/project.mbt` (exports and the symbol table)
- Create: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/resolve/scope.mbt` (imports, default imports, resolution)
- Create: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/resolve/references.mbt` (the body walker with locals)
- Create: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/resolve/errors.mbt`
- Test: `pkgs/morphir-elm/frontend/resolve/resolve_test.mbt`

**Interfaces:**
- Consumes: `ParsedModule` (Task 2); `@mapping.ElmCore`, `@mapping.elm_name`, `@mapping.elm_path`, `@mapping.elm_core_modules` (Task 1); `@sdk_spec.sdk_specification()`, `@sdk_spec.sdk_package_name()`.
- Produces (package `finos/morphir-elm/frontend/resolve`, alias `@resolve`):
  - `pub(all) struct ResolveProblem { code : String, message : String, path : String, range : @ast.Range? } derive(Eq, Debug)`
  - `pub(all) suberror ResolveFailed { ResolveFailed(Array[ResolveProblem]) }`
  - `pub(all) suberror ResolveError { ResolveError(String, String) }` — (code, message) for one name; callers add the range.
  - `pub struct Project` with `pub fn Project::new(Array[String], Array[ParsedModule]) -> Project raise ResolveFailed` (package segments, modules). It checks every exposing list and every import.
  - `pub fn Project::scope(Self, Array[String]) -> Scope` (module name)
  - `pub fn Project::fqname(Self, Array[String], String) -> @ir.FQName` (module name, local Elm name)
  - `pub fn Project::exports(Self, Array[String]) -> Exports`
  - `pub(all) struct Exports { all : Bool, values : Map[String, Bool], types : Map[String, Bool] }` — `types[name] = true` when the constructors are exported (`T(..)`), `false` when only the type is exported (`T`).
  - `pub fn Scope::resolve_type(Self, Array[String], String) -> @ir.FQName raise ResolveError` (qualifier, name)
  - `pub fn Scope::resolve_value(Self, Array[String], String, (String) -> Bool) -> Resolved raise ResolveError` (qualifier, name, is-local)
  - `pub fn Scope::resolve_operator(Self, String) -> @ir.FQName raise ResolveError`
  - `pub(all) enum Resolved { Local(String); Global(@ir.FQName) } derive(Eq, Debug)`
  - `pub fn Project::references(Self, Array[String]) -> Array[Array[String]] raise ResolveFailed` — the project modules that the declarations of a module reference, by dotted name (each once, in first-use order), from type annotations, type definitions, value bodies and patterns.

**Resolution rules (spec section 4):**
- Exports come from the exposing list: `exposing (..)` exports everything (types with constructors); `T` exports an opaque type; `T(..)` exports the type and its constructors; a type alias is exported by `TypeOrAliasExpose`. An exposing entry that names no declaration of the module is `elm.unresolved_name` at that entry.
- Unqualified value: a local (the callback says yes), then a top-level value or constructor of this module, then a name that an import exposes, then the default imports. Two imports that expose the same name, both found at this step, are `elm.ambiguous_name` when the name is used.
- Unqualified type: a type of this module, then a type that an import exposes, then the default imports.
- Qualified name `Q.name`: `Q` is an import alias or a full module name of an import (or a default import). Then the name must be exported by that module.
- Default imports (Elm 0.19.1): `Basics` exposing everything; `List` exposing `List` and `(::)`; `Maybe` exposing `Maybe(Just, Nothing)`; `Result` exposing `Result(Ok, Err)`; `String` exposing `String`; `Char` exposing `Char`; `Tuple`; `Debug`; `Platform` exposing `Program`; `Platform.Cmd` as `Cmd` exposing `Cmd`; `Platform.Sub` as `Sub` exposing `Sub`.
- Elm core module names resolve through `ElmCore`. `Basics` exposing everything means every `Basics.*` entry of the table plus the operators. A core value with no table entry is `elm.unsupported_value` and the message names it (`List.foldl2`). `Debug.*`, `Platform`, `Cmd` and `Sub` names are `elm.unsupported`.
- `Morphir.SDK.<M>` imports resolve against `@sdk_spec.sdk_specification()`: module path `elm_path([M])`, type and value names by `elm_name`. A name that the SDK module does not have is `elm.unresolved_name`.
- An import of a module that is not a project module, not an Elm core module and not a `Morphir.SDK.*` module is `elm.unsupported_module` at the import.

