```moonbit
///| Internal types. `Con` names are canonical FQName text.
priv enum Ty {
  Meta(Int)
  Rigid(String)                         // declared variable, canonical name
  Gen(Int)                              // quantified variable inside a Poly
  Con(String, Array[Ty])
  Fun(Ty, Ty)
  Tup(Array[Ty])
  Rec(Map[String, Ty], Ty?)             // canonical field names; tail is Meta/Rigid; None = closed
  UnitTy
} derive(Eq, Debug)

priv enum MetaState {
  Unbound(level~ : Int, classes~ : Array[String])
  Link(Ty)
}

priv struct Poly { gens : Array[Array[String]], body : Ty }   // gens[i] = classes of Gen(i)

priv suberror Mismatch { Mismatch(String, Ty, Ty) }           // code, expected, found

priv struct Solver {
  metas : Array[MetaState]
  rigid_classes : Map[String, Array[String]]
  expand : (String, Array[Ty]) -> Ty?                         // alias expansion; None = nominal
}
```

  - `fn Solver::new(expand : (String, Array[Ty]) -> Ty?) -> Solver`
  - `fn Solver::fresh(self, level : Int, classes : Array[String]) -> Ty`
  - `fn Solver::prune(self, t : Ty) -> Ty` (follows links; flattens `Rec` tails that are `Rec`)
  - `fn Solver::unify(self, expected : Ty, found : Ty) -> Unit raise Mismatch`
  - `fn join(a : Array[String], b : Array[String]) -> Array[String]?` in `classes.mbt`
  - `pub(all) struct InferenceProblem { code : String, node : String, message : String, expected : @ir.Type?, found : @ir.Type?, source : @ir.SourceLocation? } derive(Eq, Debug)`
  - `pub(all) suberror InferenceFailed { InferenceFailed(Array[InferenceProblem]) } derive(Eq, Debug)`

**Class rules (exact):**

`join` is commutative:

| Inputs | Result |
| --- | --- |
| `[]` and any `x` | `x` |
| `x` and `x` | `x` |
| `comparable` and `appendable` | `compappend` |
| `number` and `comparable` | `number` |
| `compappend` and `comparable` | `compappend` |
| `compappend` and `appendable` | `compappend` |
| any other pair (`number` with `appendable`, `number` with `compappend`) | `None` |

A class set is stored with at most one element.

Instances:

| Class | Satisfied by |
| --- | --- |
| `number` | `Con("morphir/SDK:basics#int")` and `Con("…basics#float")` |
| `comparable` | int, float, `char#char`, `string#string`, `list#list` with a comparable element, `Tup` of 2 or 3 comparables |
| `appendable` | `string#string`, `list#list` with any element |
| `compappend` | `string#string`, `list#list` with a comparable element |

A `Rigid` satisfies a class when its own declared class (`rigid_classes`, filled from the name prefix) joins to
that same class. For example, a rigid `number` satisfies `comparable`.

**Unification (exact semantics):**
- Two metas: merge the classes with `join` (`no_instance` if `None`), take the lower level, link one to the other.
- Meta and a type: occurs check (`occurs`), level adjustment of the metas inside the type, check the meta's class
  against the type (`no_instance`), then link.
- `Rigid a` and `Rigid a`: success. A rigid against any other non-meta type: `rigid_variable`.
- `Con`: if the names differ, try `expand` on either side and retry. Then the names and arities must be equal and
  the arguments unify; otherwise `type_mismatch`.
- `Fun`, `Tup` (equal length) and `UnitTy` unify structurally.
- `Rec(f1, t1)` with `Rec(f2, t2)` (row rules from the spec):

| Tails | Rule |
| --- | --- |
| both closed | the field sets must be equal |
| `Some(r1)` with closed | the fields in `f1` only must be empty (else `missing_field`); `r1 := Rec(f2 only, None)` |
| closed with `Some(r2)` | the mirror case |
| `Some(r1)` with `Some(r2)` | fresh row `ρ`; `r1 := Rec(f2 only, Some(ρ))`; `r2 := Rec(f1 only, Some(ρ))`. If `r1 == r2` after pruning and either only-set is not empty, `type_mismatch`. |

  The common fields unify.
- The `Mismatch` code is one of `type_mismatch`, `occurs`, `rigid_variable`, `no_instance` or `missing_field`. It
  carries the two pruned types.

