end
</code></pre></details></figure><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Gate</th><th>Required evidence</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Profile semantics</td><td>Multiple declarations, forward calls, private helpers, zero-argument calls, nested lets, shadowing and short circuiting. Fixtures have bounded Boolean parameter sets; exhaust all combinations for every public entry and record expected row counts before running.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Rejection</td><td>Duplicate declarations/parameters, unknown names, local non-callable shadows, wrong arity/type, bare function references, direct/indirect cycles, unsupported imports/effects/types, missing final expressions and recovered syntax. Type-invalid source must also be rejected by the original compiler. Valid but excluded MoonBit must get a profile rejection.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Visibility and typing</td><td>Separate consumers can call public functions and cannot name private helpers. All-private libraries have no public entry. Assert reference/intermediate application types, unique local binders and metadata ownership. Verify no call-tree expansion; Boolean outcomes alone do not prove evaluation order or bounded lowering.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Compatibility</td><td>Keep the existing seed API, stage sequence and byte-identical canonical IR/metadata receipts for valid unchanged seed fixtures. Preserve diagnostics except where a separately reviewed compiler-validity correction is required. Language selection remains moonbit; optional profile selection and capability summaries identify the accepted subset. Current and supported historical Morphir JSON inputs still work in downstream generator gates.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Ion and JSON boundaries</td><td>Ion text/binary checkpoints preserve all entry types, origins and provenance. The existing explicit JSON-only component retains the native rich envelope. Lossy Morphir JSON export must fail explicitly or use a documented supported policy; do not silently strip library metadata.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Observation and cancellation</td><td>Phase parentage and exactly one terminal outcome on success/failure/cancellation. No-op performs no clock/ID/sink work. Sink failures do not change IR, diagnostics or checkpoints. Dry-run reads no source bodies and creates no files.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Limits and determinism</td><td>Boundary/over-bound cases for bytes, declarations, aggregate expressions, call sites, lets and graph depth. Stable phase/source-order diagnostics and canonical public-entry ordering; cancellations during collection, resolution, graph checks and lowering. Do not compare duration or random trace IDs as deterministic artifacts.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Installed execution</td><td>Clean working directory and packed npm package. Required JS, Wasm GC and native C lanes in debug/release, plus separately pinned LLVM on supported darwin/arm64. Required lanes fail when unavailable; compile, invoke all public entries, compare, dispose and retain identities.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p>Pure tests and CLI compatibility checks run on all existing MoonBit targets, including WASI. Preserve the current local-logging capability limits on standalone WASI/Wasm GC hosts. Local and hosted required lanes retain source, parser, profile, compiler/core, SDK, runtime and invocation identities. A completed local library gate does not prove upstream extension installation.</p></section><section id="delivery"><div class="section-no">10 / A7</div><h2>Deliver small, reviewable slices</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Slice</th><th>Concrete result</th><th>Gate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>F0, this study</td><td>Pinned parser probe, semantic risks, metadata-hook design and HTML diagrams.</td><td>Six tests on four targets, compiler type-error check, offline HTML QA. No frontend implementation claim.</td></tr><tr><td>F1, Boolean library</td><td>Pure parser adapter, profile checker and one-function typed IR lowering.</td><td>Truth-table comparison against original source and Scheme; malformed/unsupported input rejection.</td></tr><tr><td>F2, engine registration</td><td>Metadata-aware source contract, legacy frontend adaptation, CLI configuration and Ion checkpoints.</td><td>Preserve origins through codecs/components, dry-run and all output modes; no regressions to existing frontends.</td></tr><tr><td>F3, installed execution</td><td>Boolean source model generated and executed through landed E1/E2.</td><td>Required supported target matrix, bounded cleanup, installed package receipts and instrumentation neutrality.</td></tr><tr><td>F4, A2-dependent packaging</td><td>Publish the agreed extension manifest/bundle and verify host installation.</td><td>Wait for A2 contract; independent upstream Rust and component acceptance, if selected.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3>Next local library slices</h3><p>L1 landed in <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/48">PR #48</a>, squash <code>7bbf25291529783aedd9477af33706a761a8f8e6</code>, on 7 October 2026. L2 landed in <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/50">PR #50</a>, squash <code>4900f4d</code>, after all 19 checks passed. L3 landed in <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/55">PR #55</a> under plan <code>morphir-ukvn.1.10.9</code>, squash commit <code>67bea18dc8f07543639c7b3c41335c1de0e317c9</code>, after all merge-queue checks passed with maintainer approval.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Slice and status</th><th>Result</th><th>Landing gate</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>L1, pure library compiler<br>Merged in PR #48</td><td>Add the opt-in library API, pure phase contracts, multi-function resolution, Boolean checking, acyclic graph validation and typed lowering.</td><td>All-target focused tests, original compiler differential fixtures, limits, scope/visibility and seed compatibility. The pure profile gate passed before L2 registration.</td></tr><tr><td>L2, adapter and CLI<br><span class="tag">Qualified locally; PR #50 open</span></td><td>Separate language, provider and profile selection in generic registration/planning; expose both profiles under moonbit with capability summaries and public-entry behavior.</td><td>Lazy profile selection, mixed-profile projects, claim-driven capabilities and named rejection; Ion/JSON preservation, build validation, multi-entry execution and neutral observations.</td></tr><tr><td>L3, installed qualification</td><td>Run original/Scheme/generated library parity from the installed CLI on required targets and hosts.</td><td>All public entry rows, debug/release, pinned LLVM where supported, consumer privacy, failed sinks, cancellation/cleanup and identity receipts.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><div class="callout"><strong>L1 local qualification · 7 October 2026</strong><p>27 focused tests pass on each of four targets. The compiler gate passes 86 rows per target/mode: 44 unchanged seed rows plus 42 library rows on JS, native, Wasm and Wasm GC in debug/release. It rejects all 16 external private-symbol probes, checks five compiler-invalid sources, and distinguishes compiler-valid recursion excluded by the profile. Seed source, IR and generated-artifact hashes remain identical. Full workspace tests pass 829 Wasm, 829 Wasm GC, 838 JS and 837 native cases. Required lint, formatting and package validation pass.</p><p><a href="../a7-l1-library/identity.json">Compiler and dependency identities</a> · <a href="../a7-l1-library/library-models.json">Library fixture sources and artifacts</a> · <a href="../a7-l1-library/seed-compatibility.json">Seed compatibility receipt</a>. Plan <code>morphir-ukvn.1.10.7</code> tracks L1; L1 is closed; plan <code>morphir-ukvn.1.10.8</code> tracks L2. L3 is closed and merged; A2-dependent F4 remains open.</p></div><div class="callout"><h3>L2 local qualification · 7 October 2026</h3><p>Original L2 qualification at <code>fa95140</code>: selection and adapter tests pass 37 and 11 cases per target. Workspace tests pass 841 Wasm, 841 Wasm GC, 850 JavaScript and 849 native cases. CLI checks pass all four hosts and installed npm, including public/private execution entry selection and required compiler validation. The original/compiler/Scheme/generated gate retains 86 rows per target and mode with unchanged seed and library fixture identities. Existing installed lifecycle passes 24 model/format lanes of 23 calls each plus eight seed source lanes of four Boolean rows on JS, Wasm GC, native C and archive-pinned LLVM in debug/release. Lint, format and package validation pass.</p><p><a href="../a7-l2-selection/qualification.json">Qualification receipt</a> · <a href="../a7-l2-selection/installed/summary.json">Installed compatibility gate</a> · <a href="../a7-l2-selection/seed-compatibility.json">Unchanged fixture identities</a> · <a href="../a7-l2-selection/selection.svg">Selection SVG</a>. <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/50">PR #50</a> at <code>fa9514013f41537753c3372c3e6c284d888129ab</code> records the original qualification snapshot. Checked L2 head was <code>4c9625d</code>; merged main is <code>4900f4d</code>. Full installed library parity landed in L3; A7 and A2-dependent F4 remain open.</p></div><div class="callout"><h3>Continuation · 8 October 2026</h3><p>Current main <code>a290730</code> adds shared workbench invocation admission. Maintainer authorization allows basing L2 on <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/53">PR #53</a>, which supplies the private-function fixture correction. L2 is based on its head <code>0168a4d</code>, at <code>4c9625d</code>. Workspace tests now pass 861 Wasm, 861 Wasm GC, 870 JavaScript and 869 native cases; required lint, format and package validation pass. CLI qualification passes on all four hosts and installed npm. Installed lifecycle passes all 24 model/format lanes and eight seed source lanes on JS, Wasm GC, native C and archive-pinned LLVM in debug/release. <a href="../a7-l2-selection/installed-pr53/summary.json">Rebased installed compatibility receipt</a>. PR #53 landed as <code>a32a021</code>. L2 then squash merged as <code>4900f4d</code> on 8 October after maintainer authorization. <a href="../a7-l2-selection/pr53-continuation.json">Continuation receipt</a>. <a href="../a7-l2-selection/merge.json">Merge receipt</a> records 19 passing checks and no review threads.</p></div><h3>Separate dependencies</h3><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Work</th><th>Depends on</th><th>Next requirement</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td>Boolean library, L1-L3</td><td>No A2 or shared-inference dependency</td><td>L1 library lowering, L2 adapter/CLI selection and L3 installed qualification are landed. Next, settle readable naming and declaration-owned linked targetNames facts; F4 waits for A2.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Richer source typing</td><td>Shared inference<br><code>morphir-ukvn.5.22.2</code></td><td>Coordinate reusable IR typing and define MoonBit-specific semantics.</td></tr>
<tr><td>Multi-file linking</td><td>A separate project-compilation design</td><td><ul><li>Complete host-owned source snapshot</li><li>Public interfaces and dependency inventory</li><li>Unit aggregation and deterministic module graph</li></ul></td></tr>
<tr><td>F4 extension delivery<br><code>morphir-ukvn.1.10.5</code></td><td>A2 packaging contract<br><code>morphir-ukvn.1.3</code></td><td>Agree the bundle and guest boundary. Verify install, describe, initialize, compile and generate in an independently pinned upstream host.</td></tr>
<tr><td>WIT component route</td><td>B2 contracts and B3 host support, both open</td><td>Prove component compatibility through host acceptance. Keep Extism compatibility for existing installs.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div><p class="footnote">Extension delivery preserves Ion internally and uses an explicit checked transport boundary. A native or WASI build does not establish component compatibility.</p><p>Numeric, compound-type, package-linking and effect profiles follow as separately scoped work after F1-F3. A7 remains open until its source-model and extension-delivery acceptance are satisfied. F1 is tracked as <code>morphir-ukvn.1.10.2</code>. Its pure package and compiler gate landed in <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/38">PR #38</a>, squash commit <code>2e8f8e50ae0f6a5b7540495fe42245fc21304ac7</code>, with all 20 checks passing. The compiler gate compares 11 original models and generated libraries against 44 independently expected Boolean outcomes and Scheme on JS, native, Wasm and Wasm GC in debug and release. It also found and fixed nested-condition parentheses in the existing generator. F2 landed in <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/40">PR #40</a>, squash <code>32f2033d86ddffe98735bed3d407a2540f6f23a1</code>, after all 20 checks passed and no unresolved review threads remained, on <code>DamianReeves/morphir-a7-engine</code> and tracked as <code>morphir-ukvn.1.10.3</code>. Its focused engine/adapter tests pass 28 cases on each of four targets in debug and release. Full workspace tests pass 723 Wasm, 723 Wasm GC, 730 JS and 729 native cases. CLI source/checkpoint/generation cases pass on all four hosts and the installed npm package. Required lint, format and package validation gates pass. Compiler-provider regression passes, including 60 execution fault cases and rich pricing parity on JS, Wasm GC and native in debug/release. F3 landed in <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/41">PR #41</a>, squash <code>b1a02987806bc6e58d8800f7b4bb823b2fbd693c</code>, after all 19 exact-head checks passed and no unresolved review threads remained, tracked as <code>morphir-ukvn.1.10.4</code>. It extends installed npm acceptance with CLI source lowering, binary Ion checkpoints and four Boolean rows compared against the original compiler, independent expectations, Scheme and generated execution. Required lanes include JS, Wasm GC and native C, plus hash-pinned LLVM on darwin/arm64, in debug and release. The full installed gate passes all four required targets in debug and release. Its 24 existing model/format lanes pass 23 cases each; the source model passes four Boolean rows in eight lanes against the original compiler, independent expectations, Scheme and generated execution. Instrumentation neutrality, failed optional sinks, dry-run, framing, mismatch rejection and lease disposal pass. An additional LLVM-only run verifies configurable target selection and explicitly observed sink failure. Repository lint, format and package validation pass. F4 remains A2-blocked. Independent observation follow-up <code>morphir-ukvn.1.10.6</code> landed in PR #43. It adds portable frontend scopes and <code>--log</code> defaults with explicit path overrides. Source/checkpoint privacy, failure/cancellation terminals and sink neutrality pass. Installed acceptance passes 24 existing model/format lanes and eight source lanes on JS, Wasm GC, native C and pinned LLVM in debug/release; 60 execution faults pass. CLI checks pass native, Node, Wasm, Wasm GC and installed npm. The HTML passes offline checks across four widths and both themes. The follow-up landed in <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/43">PR #43</a>, squash commit <code>1206065c333b4f11d69130f17cd4d94c54c437e5</code>, merged 2026-10-04T16:43:33Z after maintainer approval. Its reviewed head was <code>f805ae0ea228d01de414e32bbcb6171202076e1f</code>, rebased onto <code>40587e6</code>. Final workspace tests pass 737 Wasm, 737 Wasm GC, 746 JS and 745 native. All 20 checks pass on that head, CI run <code>37215900387</code>, with no unresolved review threads. Installed CI receipts verify six Linux source lanes and eight macOS lanes including pinned LLVM, all four frontend stages and identical binary checkpoint identities across hosts. <a href="../a7-observe-ci/acceptance.json">Local CI acceptance receipt</a> retains the checks. The task is closed with merge and validation evidence. A7 remains open; F4 extension delivery still depends on A2. This design is stored in beads.</p></section><section id="naming"><h2>Readable names and upstream targetNames facts</h2><p>Ordinary public names should remain readable. Normalize source spelling into Morphir words and initialisms, preserve exact source origins, and allocate escapes only for ambiguity, binding hygiene or target constraints. Retain original source spelling, requested target spelling and actual allocation separately. Recoverable normalization and automatic target conflicts warn and continue with traceable names and actionable fixes; ordinary fresh-variable allocation stays quiet. Exact target requests retain their spelling and conflicting requests fail. An optional strict naming policy can promote recovery warnings before publication. Follow finos/morphir’s <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir/blob/23e7dfa4202d45fe74ef05e5214c0890125325d6/docs/design/draft/ir/linked-metadata.md">scoped linked-metadata design</a> and <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir/blob/23e7dfa4202d45fe74ef05e5214c0890125325d6/kb/bundles/morphir/morphir-ir/decisions/0019-native-metadata-uses-a-scoped-property-graph.md">Decision 0019</a>. The typed <code>targetNames</code> fact has separate frontend/backend maps keyed by language ID, including <code>moonbit</code>. This supersedes the proposed standalone <code>moonbit.targetName</code> property as the semantic contract.</p><p>Carry that scoped fact in declaration-owned <code>IRUnit.metadata</code> through existing Ion checkpoints. The generator must resolve the predicate, validate its type and language-ID interpretation, and consume <code>backend.moonbit</code> through one allocated symbol table shared with references, invocations and manifests. A native V4.1 projection uses the right carrier and portable Node URI, including explicit-subject <code>$meta.@graph</code> for value definitions, rather than assigning declaration metadata to a body expression.</p><p>Current engine storage is separate from native V4.1 JSON/YAML/Ion support. Keep V4.0 behavior and the existing JSON loss guard; a checked native adapter may later preserve facts in JSON. Unknown data, assertion ownership and existing decorator overlays remain intact. Local storage or parser validation does not establish trusted semantics or MCK qualification.</p><p><a href="morphir-moonbit-naming.html">Read the revised naming proposal, upstream entry table, metadata shape and SVG allocation diagram</a>. Sources are pinned to upstream <code>23e7dfa</code>; <code>morphir-uqub.6</code>, <code>morphir-uqub.11</code> and <code>morphir-d7e8</code> retain the shared metadata work. Naming behavior remains proposed; PR #55 qualifies the current encoding.</p></section><section id="decisions"><div class="section-no">11 / A7</div><h2>Fix the first library scope before implementation</h2><div class="decision"><div class="decision-id">D1</div><div><h3>Separate language, provider and profile</h3><p>Keep <code>moonbit</code> as the language. Propose <code>moonbit-model-bool-library-v1</code> as an optional profile selection under the same provider, with advertised capabilities and evidence status. Keep the existing seed default and API unchanged. The source is one file and one logical module, with all functions checked before publication.</p></div></div><div class="decision"><div class="decision-id">D2</div><div><h3>Allow direct calls and immutable locals, reject cycles</h3><p>Collect explicit signatures first, resolve lexical names with distinct binder identities, then check fully applied Boolean calls and the whole call graph. Preserve forward calls, local shadowing and same-module private access. No imports, recursion, function values or general inference.</p></div></div><div class="decision"><div class="decision-id">D3</div><div><h3>Produce a library without an implicit entry</h3><p>Add LibraryOutput with a canonical list of public entries. Reuse typed IR and generated manifest contracts. Private-only source can compile; requests to execute private or absent entries fail. Do not break the seed's single-entry output.</p></div></div><div class="decision"><div class="decision-id">D4</div><div><h3>Retain pins and prove every claimed construct</h3><p>Keep parser 0.4.1 and matching compiler/core acceptance identities. The design probe verifies the proposed source syntax against the compiler; L1 differential acceptance passes locally; L3 installed library qualification passes locally and in the merge queue, and is landed in PR #55. Conformance must cover the full advertised profile, all public entry rows, generated visibility and all required host lanes.</p></div></div><div class="decision"><div class="decision-id">D5</div><div><h3>Reuse shared typing only when the profile needs it</h3><p>The Boolean checker assigns known Bool/function types and does not wait for <code>morphir-ukvn.5.22.2</code>. Richer types and generic inference get a separate design with that reusable service. Width/overflow semantics remain source-specific responsibilities.</p></div></div><div class="decision"><div class="decision-id">D6</div><div><h3>Keep extension delivery independently tracked</h3><p>F4 depends on A2's common layout and packaging command. The roadmap selects WIT/component hosts; B2/B3 establish those contracts. Current upstream packaging evidence uses Extism claims and is not proof that a MoonBit WASI artifact is compatible. Transport must use an explicit checked boundary around rich Ion metadata. A7 remains open; release/publication requires its own authorization.</p></div></div><div class="callout open"><strong>Next integration checks</strong><p>Define typed language/provider/profile descriptors and claim-driven selection without a language alias; align fine-grained support with the shared vocabulary. L1 verifies let/call syntax, zero-argument/private-helper lowering, unique binders and native Ion origins through Scheme and the generator. If a required construct fails, report it and revise its admission rule before advertising the profile. The budgets above are enforced hard caps, not measured performance claims.</p></div></section><section id="sources"><div class="section-no">12 / A7</div><h2>Evidence and scope</h2><ul class="refs"><li><a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/37">Landed E2, PR #37</a>, main snapshot <code>79d4d05e0fdae00b8dc9a29feee3dd898dcf6694</code>.</li><li><a href="../../pkgs/morphir-engine/source_providers.mbt">L2 typed provider registry and lazy selection</a>; <a href="../../pkgs/morphir-engine/moonbit/adapter.mbt">seed and library adapters</a>; <a href="../../apps/morphir/output.mbt">descriptor-driven human and structured planning output</a>. Current commits <code>f3b530e</code>, <code>0f08ce7</code>, <code>6d88424</code> and <code>4c9625d</code> record the implementation and public contracts.</li><li><a href="../../pkgs/morphir-engine/types.mbt">Current source frontend registration</a>; <a href="../../pkgs/morphir-engine/plan.mbt">planned pipeline</a> wraps legacy IRFile and routes rich units.</li><li><a href="../../pkgs/morphir-engine/data/types.mbt">IRUnit metadata and provenance</a>; <a href="../../pkgs/morphir-engine/data/registry.mbt">Ion defaults and Morphir JSON loss guards</a>.</li><li><a href="../../pkgs/morphir-engine/generation.mbt">Generator unit adapter</a>; <a href="../../pkgs/morphir-moonbit/README.md">current generator profile and exact-number/UTF-16 mapping</a>.</li><li><a href="https://github.com/moonbitlang/parser">Official parser repository</a>. Published archive 0.4.1 and isolated probe live in <a href="../a7-feasibility/identity.json">local identity receipt</a>.</li><li><a href="../a7-feasibility/probe/probe_test.mbt">Six probe cases</a>; <a href="../a7-feasibility/bad-source/bad.mbt">negative compiler fixture</a>. Compiler help and logs are local evidence, not a public typed-AST contract.</li><li><a href=".assets/a7-ecosystem-20261004/identity.json">Pinned ecosystem evidence</a> retains committed protocol and decisions at <code>5c5307d89f34d876e8f1ebf561ec55efbadf9fa0</code>; the profile selector remains a local proposal. <a href="../../CONTEXT.md">Local glossary</a> records the language/provider/profile distinction.</li><li><a href=".assets/a7-library-20261007/library-phases.finalize-summary.json">Implemented pure data-flow specification and artifact receipt</a>, with validation, strict artifact checks and browser gate passing; <a href=".assets/a7-library-20261007/library-phases.browser-check.json">browser evidence</a>.</li><li><a href="../../pkgs/morphir-moonbit-frontend/types.mbt">Seed API and limits</a>; <a href="../../pkgs/morphir-engine/source_frontends.mbt">registration, identity validation and lazy descriptors</a>; <a href="../../pkgs/morphir-moonbit/expressions.mbt">reference, application and local-definition lowering</a>; <a href="../../pkgs/morphir-moonbit/lowered_types.mbt">curried expression construction</a>. Evidence snapshot <code>1206065c333b4f11d69130f17cd4d94c54c437e5</code>.</li><li>Beads: <code>morphir-ukvn.1.10</code>, study <code>morphir-ukvn.1.10.1</code>. A2 blocker <code>morphir-ukvn.1.3</code>. Workbench and Rust umbrella work retain separate ownership/completion.</li><li><a href="../a7-f3-installed/moonbit-source/summary.json">Installed source acceptance receipt</a>; <a href="../a7-f3-llvm-config/moonbit-source/summary.json">LLVM-only selection and sink-failure evidence</a>.</li></ul><p class="footnote">Local review artifact. F1 production source is in <a href="../../pkgs/morphir-moonbit-frontend/README.md">the Boolean frontend package</a>. <a href="../frontend-acceptance/identity.json">Compiler acceptance identities</a> and <a href="../frontend-acceptance/models.json">source, IR and generated artifacts</a> record the current implementation. The seed frontend, engine registration, installed source acceptance and observations are landed. Pure library phases landed in PR #48; engine/CLI profile selection landed in PR #50; L3 installed qualification landed in PR #55, squash 67bea18dc8f07543639c7b3c41335c1de0e317c9, at 2026-10-08T15:01:30Z. Naming changes are proposed; A2 extension delivery remains unfinished. Diagram checks and browser QA do not prove semantic correctness.</p></section><footer>Revision 0.17 records merged L1/L2/L3 and a naming proposal aligned with upstream linked metadata, traceable recovery and structured warnings. F0 is complete; F1, F2 and F3 landed in PRs #38, #40 and #41, and frontend instrumentation landed in PR #43. E2 is merged; A7 remains open and final extension delivery depends on A2.</footer></main></div><script src=".assets/mermaid-12.0.0.min.js"></script><script>window.diagramReady=(async()=>{const dark=matchMedia('(prefers-color-scheme: dark)').matches;mermaid.initialize({startOnLoad:false,securityLevel:'strict',theme:'base',themeVariables:{primaryColor:dark?'#203a2d':'#e8f3ed',primaryTextColor:dark?'#e2eee7':'#172c24',primaryBorderColor:dark?'#72d3a9':'#096348',lineColor:dark?'#b0c0b7':'#53665e',secondaryColor:dark?'#392d20':'#fff3e2',tertiaryColor:dark?'#1c231f':'#fff',actorBkg:dark?'#203a2d':'#e8f3ed',actorTextColor:dark?'#e2eee7':'#172c24',signalColor:dark?'#b0c0b7':'#53665e',signalTextColor:dark?'#e2eee7':'#172c24',noteBkgColor:dark?'#392d20':'#fff3e2',noteTextColor:dark?'#e2eee7':'#172c24'},flowchart:{htmlLabels:false,useMaxWidth:true},sequence:{useMaxWidth:true,wrap:true}});for(const f of document.querySelectorAll('.diagram')){const r=await mermaid.render(f.id+'-svg',f.querySelector('.mermaid-source').textContent);f.querySelector('.diagram-render').innerHTML=r.svg;}document.documentElement.dataset.diagrams='ready';})().catch(e=>{document.documentElement.data