</style></head><body><a class="skip" href="#main">Skip to design</a><div class="shell"><aside class="sidebar"><div class="brand">Morphir / A7</div><div class="meta">Source frontend and extension<br>Revision 0.23 · 9 October 2026</div><nav aria-label="Design sections"><a href="#outcome">01 · Bring a MoonBit model into the same pipeline</a><a href="#evidence">02 · What the feasibility probe proves</a><a href="#pipeline">03 · Keep each stage independently replaceable</a><a href="#contracts">04 · Make the pure frontend return a rich unit</a><a href="#profile">05 · Grow the seed into a Boolean library</a><a href="#ion">06 · Use Ion internally and preserve JSON compatibility</a><a href="#host">07 · Keep capabilities and instrumentation explicit</a><a href="#cli">08 · Integrate through the existing command and plan surface</a><a href="#acceptance">09 · Compare original source with the lowered model</a><a href="#delivery">10 · Deliver the library and extension separately</a><a href="#naming">Naming · Readable identities and target attributes</a><a href="#decisions">11 · Resolve these before widening implementation</a><a href="#sources">12 · Evidence and scope</a></nav></aside><main id="main"><div class="eyebrow">Next roadmap capability</div><h1>MoonBit source to typed Morphir models</h1><p class="lead">A landed pure Boolean library compiler and implemented provider/profile selection, with installed library qualification landed and readable frontend identities landed in PR #59 and shared readable target allocation landed in PR #60 and scoped target-name fact consumption landed in PR #61.</p><section id="outcome"><div class="section-no">01 / A7</div><h2>Grow source support on the landed pipeline</h2><p class="lead">The next local capability is a single-file Boolean library: several explicitly typed functions, immutable local bindings and direct calls. It feeds the existing typed IR, Ion checkpoint, MoonBit generator, build and verification stages.</p><div class="callout"><strong>Landed foundation</strong><p>E1/E2 generate, build and execute libraries. F1/F2/F3 add the single-function MoonBit frontend, engine/CLI integration and installed acceptance. Frontend instrumentation and default logs landed in <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/43">PR #43</a>, squash <code>1206065</code>. The L1 branch starts from current main <code>730734b</code>, including the Elm generator and Workbench changes.</p></div><div class="callout open"><strong>L1 landed · PR #48 merged</strong><p>The additive pure API <code>compile_library</code>, implemented in <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/48">PR #48</a>, squash <code>7bbf252</code> with qualification <code>90a72b1</code>, implements <code>moonbit-model-bool-library-v1</code> and extends source admission without changing the existing <code>moonbit-model-bool-v1</code> contract. It accepts one immutable source file and one logical module. Project discovery, multi-file linking, richer source types and installable extension delivery remain separate capabilities.</p></div><p>A useful example is a public eligibility function calling a private helper. This exercises declarations, scope, typed references, visibility and library entry selection without introducing numeric overflow, effects or recursion. The library slice can proceed independently of A2 packaging. F4 remains blocked on the agreed extension bundle and guest boundary.</p></section><section id="evidence"><div class="section-no">02 / A7</div><h2>What the feasibility probe proves</h2><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Probe</th><th>Observed result</th><th>Design consequence</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Published parser 0.4.1</td><td>Six focused tests pass on JS, native, WASI and Wasm GC with compiler 0.10.14+7d59c7ec9.</td><td>A portable parser candidate exists. F1 adopts the audited pinned parser. Broader parser conformance remains a separate gate.</td></tr><tr><td>Boolean signature with an Int body</td><td>Parser reports no syntax error. The compiler rejects it with diagnostic 4014.</td><td>Syntax acceptance cannot establish a typed Morphir model.</td></tr><tr><td>Mutable local variable</td><td>Parser accepts the syntax.</td><td>A semantic profile must reject or deliberately lower effects.</td></tr><tr><td>Broken conditional</td><td>Parser reports recovery diagnostics.</td><td>Recovered AST nodes cannot be published as a valid model.</td></tr><tr><td>Int maximum + 1</td><td>The probe returns -2147483648 on all four tested targets.</td><td>Mapping source Int arithmetic directly to exact Morphir Integer arithmetic changes behavior.</td></tr><tr><td>Boolean seed</td><td>All four truth-table cases pass in the original MoonBit source.</td><td>F1 compares 11 source models, Scheme and generated libraries on four targets in debug and release. F3 adds installed CLI execution evidence.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>The parser's upstream README identifies it as experimental. Pin version, source identity and archive identity; do not depend on a moving repository head. All 345 archive files match the corresponding cached source bytes used by the probe. Cache source identity and archive identity are recorded separately.</p><details><summary>Probe identity</summary><pre><code>{
