Yoorkin/ArgParser 0.2.1; all four targets, standalone WASI imports, installed npm and execution acceptance pass, bc1127c; morphir-ukvn.5.19.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done · E2 Task 4 lifecycle, cleanup and failure/publication guarantees, PR #34 / 9ce5127; integrated at 258471c."><span>Done · E2 Task 4 lifecycle, cleanup and failure/publication guarantees, PR #34 / 9ce5127; integrated at 258471c.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done · E2 Task 5 independent semantic conformance, PR #35 / 4ede1e5; integrated at dd85ebe."><span>Done · E2 Task 5 independent semantic conformance, PR #35 / 4ede1e5; integrated at dd85ebe.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done · Land results, typed inputs, Ion, live Rust acceptance and CLI parser continuations through reviewed PR #36 / fd4026e."><span>Done · Land results, typed inputs, Ion, live Rust acceptance and CLI parser continuations through reviewed PR #36 / fd4026e.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done · Upstream typed-value schemas, examples and original 62 structural checks landed in PR #1031 / 34b1a8f; morphir-etg2.1. Host adoption remains separate."><span>Done · Upstream typed-value schemas, examples and original 62 structural checks landed in PR #1031 / 34b1a8f; morphir-etg2.1. Host adoption remains separate.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done · Shared MCK JSON/Ion decode corpus and MoonBit adapter landed in PR #1031 / 34b1a8f and PR #39 / f0cc004; 64 cases per Node/native debug/release lane and seven protocol tests on all four targets; morphir-etg2.2."><span>Done · Shared MCK JSON/Ion decode corpus and MoonBit adapter landed in PR #1031 / 34b1a8f and PR #39 / f0cc004; 64 cases per Node/native debug/release lane and seven protocol tests on all four targets; morphir-etg2.2.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done · E2 Task 6 installed lifecycle and required target matrix, PR #37 / 79d4d05; all 20 head checks passed."><span>Done · E2 Task 6 installed lifecycle and required target matrix, PR #37 / 79d4d05; all 20 head checks passed.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done · Explicit native OTLP HTTP/JSON capture and bounded delivery acceptance on Linux/macOS, PR #37 / 79d4d05. Other protocols remain unsupported."><span>Done · Explicit native OTLP HTTP/JSON capture and bounded delivery acceptance on Linux/macOS, PR #37 / 79d4d05. Other protocols remain unsupported.</span></label></li></ul></article><article class="plan-status-card"><h3>Pending and in progress</h3><ul class="plan-status-checklist"><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · Expose supported local input languages and generation backends in the shared Workbench; morphir-ukvn.5.23."><span>Pending · Expose supported local input languages and generation backends in the shared Workbench; morphir-ukvn.5.23.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · Define opt-in permissive admission for unused declarations and untaken branches; morphir-etg2.6."><span>Pending · Define opt-in permissive admission for unused declarations and untaken branches; morphir-etg2.6.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · Support entry-root reachability and tree-shaking as a separate ecosystem feature; morphir-ukvn.6."><span>Pending · Support entry-root reachability and tree-shaking as a separate ecosystem feature; morphir-ukvn.6.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="In progress · Extend and adopt the published workbench profile in finos/morphir and finos/morphir-ui. Schemas, decode and declared-value admission are merged; public-entry/invocation admission is published in green draft PRs #1035/#44. Output/outcome admission is next; SDK comparison, binary/reverse encoding, jobs and host/client adoption remain pending."><span>In progress · Extend and adopt the published workbench profile in finos/morphir and finos/morphir-ui. Schemas, decode and declared-value admission are merged; public-entry/invocation admission is published in green draft PRs #1035/#44. Output/outcome admission is next; SDK comparison, binary/reverse encoding, jobs and host/client adoption remain pending.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · Add Proton native service/provider IPC and granted workspace integration."><span>Pending · Add Proton native service/provider IPC and granted workspace integration.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · Verify a standalone browser provider for generated-code execution."><span>Pending · Verify a standalone browser provider for generated-code execution.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · Add workspace/Ion metadata-preserving UI operations and verification-backed publication."><span>Pending · Add workspace/Ion metadata-preserving UI operations and verification-backed publication.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · Cross-host recovery/replay, persistence and remaining platform packages."><span>Pending · Cross-host recovery/replay, persistence and remaining platform packages.</span></label></li></ul></article></div></div>
<p>Typed invocation is local commit <code>d850944</code>, after structured results at <code>722a126</code>. Both continuations landed in PR #36 at fd4026e. The public manifest governs admitted entries; tagged arguments use <code>morphir-invocations-v1</code>, and the shared bounded Scheme evaluator returns canonical typed values. Exact Int/Decimal, signed-zero Float64 bits, UTF-16 units, Maybe/Result, records and custom ownership have focused acceptance. Browser and packaged CEF import the pricing fixture. Typed convenience controls are complete and merged in PR #36 in morphir-ukvn.5.17. Generated-code execution and connected transport remain pending. Local IR text is retained across the JavaScript boundary for exact large-integer evaluation, inspection and export.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Stage / status</th><th scope="col">Next deliverable</th><th scope="col">Evidence to proceed</th></tr></thead><tbody>
<tr><td><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done · 01 · UI baseline delivered"><span>Done · 01 · UI baseline delivered</span></label></td><td>Retain the shared shell, explorer, generated inputs, editor components, local Scheme worker and Proton package. Keep the result-view continuation identified separately.</td><td>Existing browser/CEF workflows remain green; drafts, selection, sidebar context, cancellation, stale results and exact numbers survive integration.</td></tr>
<tr><td><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done · 02 · Adopt typed execution boundaries"><span>Done · 02 · Adopt typed execution boundaries</span></label></td><td>Local worker mode now uses ValueType/public manifests, a reusable typed-input component, custom registry, Suite/Value codecs and the portable Scheme evaluator. Typed fields and JSON share a canonical document; Ion converts through the published codec without changing exact values. Invalid conversions retain the original draft. Dynamic Scheme/worksheet remains available. Native and connected adapters remain separate pending stages.</td><td>Exact Int/Decimal, Float64 bits, UTF-16 units, Maybe/Result and constructor ownership round-trip. Generated-only restrictions remain visible without hiding inspectable declarations. The private 500-node result tree never becomes a normative wire codec.</td></tr>
<tr><td><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="In progress · 03 · Upstream transport contribution"><span>In progress · 03 · Upstream transport contribution</span></label></td><td>Update <code>morphir-etg2</code> around adoption of existing invocation/outcome profiles. Specify revision handles, jobs/cancellation, worksheet source maps, transport limits and artifact semantics; retain the real Rust v1 acceptance regression completed in morphir-ukvn.5.20.</td><td>Normative finos/morphir contribution and language-neutral fixtures; coordinated Rust/TypeScript/MoonBit adoption. New operations stay unavailable until negotiated. Current v1 methods preserve their shapes.</td></tr>
<tr><td><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · 04 · Native and generated execution adapters"><span>Pending · 04 · Native and generated execution adapters</span></label></td><td>Use engine plan/run and host-owned provider sessions through Proton IPC. Reuse compiler acquisition/pins and generated drivers. A standalone generated-code browser lane needs an explicit provider backed by verified browser embedding.</td><td>Selected capabilities and dependency snapshots match the host; no target substitution. Browser workers never import the Node/native process provider. LLVM requires its separate tested nightly/core pin and verified host. Existing Proton worker mode stays supported.</td></tr>
<tr><td><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · 05 · Workspace and publication"><span>Pending · 05 · Workspace and publication</span></label></td><td>Reuse Engine::list_projects, plan boundaries, IRUnit codecs, host grants and artifact reports. Keep source/model snapshots alongside display projections. Wait for E2 lifecycle/publication acceptance before offering verification-backed publication.</td><td>Ion metadata and identities survive processing; Morphir JSON remains supported through explicit loss-aware boundaries. Generated, validated, invoked, compared, cleaned-up and committed output have separate evidence. Failure preserves prior output.</td></tr>
<tr><td><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · 06 · Cross-host proof and hardening"><span>Pending · 06 · Cross-host proof and hardening</span></label></td><td>Run the same versioned fixture intersection through standalone, native and connected adapters; add recovery, persistence and platform package checks.</td><td>E2 Tasks 4–6 are complete and merged, including lifecycle, independent conformance, installed/debug-release CI and native OTLP HTTP/JSON collector acceptance on Linux/macOS. Shared-SDK Scheme agreement is identified accurately; cross-host adoption and other telemetry protocols remain separate. Connected durability/replay is proved separately.</td></tr>
</tbody></table></div>
    <h3>Integration rules from the merges</h3><ul>
<li>Reuse the public invocation manifest as the generated execution authority. Local generic aliases and dynamic Scheme values may remain available through their own runtime capability even when the generator rejects them.</li>
<li>Separate 200-node input forms and 500-node result display limits from execution budgets. Preserve full semantic values and Ion metadata; report unsupported or omitted presentation explicitly.</li>
<li>Exact comparison is the default. Approximate comparison requires an explicit policy and finite tolerances. Display selected target, evaluator profile and evidence; do not label shared-SDK agreement independent conformance.</li>
<li>Host-injected observations carry timing and correlation outside model/call identity. Required results bypass telemetry queues. Payload capture stays opt-in with a redactor; dropped observations cannot change a job outcome.</li>
<li>Model Result.Err, enumerated SDK model errors, validation failures, provider failures, cancellation and cleanup failures need distinct presentation. Preserve primary and cleanup causes once the E2 lifecycle contract lands.</li>
</ul>
    <h3>Acceptance checklist</h3><ul class="plan-status-checklist"><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done in browser/Proton worker mode · Switch experiences and recover each draft, selection and sidebar context."><span>Done in browser/Proton worker mode · Switch experiences and recover each draft, selection and sidebar context.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" checked disabled aria-label="Done in browser/Proton worker mode · Compile and inspect a snippet, open its compiled revision in Explorer, and run a dynamic worksheet."><span>Done in browser/Proton worker mode · Compile and inspect a snippet, open its compiled revision in Explorer, and run a dynamic worksheet.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending across all three runtimes · Open the same arithmetic distribution in standalone, native service and connected modes."><span>Pending across all three runtimes · Open the same arithmetic distribution in standalone, native service and connected modes.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending across all three runtimes · Show the same declaration, signature and original IR version."><span>Pending across all three runtimes · Show the same declaration, signature and original IR version.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending across all three runtimes · Obtain the same typed result from identical typed inputs."><span>Pending across all three runtimes · Obtain the same typed result from identical typed inputs.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending across all three runtimes · Distinguish invalid inputs, model/domain outcomes and unavailable runtime bindings."><span>Pending across all three runtimes · Distinguish invalid inputs, model/domain outcomes and unavailable runtime bindings.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending across all three runtimes · Cancel a long-running fixture and receive an authoritative terminal job outcome. Local worker cancellation is complete."><span>Pending across all three runtimes · Cancel a long-running fixture and receive an authoritative terminal job outcome. Local worker cancellation is complete.</span></label></li><li><label class="plan-status-check"><input type="checkbox" disabled aria-label="Pending · Disconnect, reconnect and inspect the original daemon job without duplicating it."><span>Pending · Disconnect, reconnect and inspect the original daemon job without duplicating it.</span></label></li></ul>
    <div class="cards"><article class="card"><h3>Build and assets</h3><p>Build the UI for JavaScript, stage its CSS and worker assets, then consume that distribution from the static web deployment, daemon asset server, and Proton package. Bundle required assets locally for standalone and installed use.</p><p>Proton's CLI/runtime/framework versions stay aligned. Match embedded compiler and dependency interfaces to the repository's pinned toolchain. Verify packages on each supported OS.</p></article><article class="card"><h3>Focused verification</h3><p>Use MoonBit checks and formatting for package boundaries and target support. Run contract scenarios against each adapter. Browser checks verify the real workflow, responsiveness, focus, and cancellation.</p><p>For desktop, include installed-package smoke checks for asset lookup, the native bridge, workspace grants, and platform editing shortcuts. Timing numbers are measured during the slice, not assumed in this design.</p></article></div>
  </section><section class="section" id="merge-readiness"><h2>Merge readiness and current main</h2><p>The maintainer approved squash merges of parent PR #1033 and MoonBit PR #42 when checks are green, including an administrator bypass where policy requires it. Main now contains <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/40">PR #40</a> at <code>32f2033</code>; merge <code>7e3fd35</code> integrates its rich MoonBit source units into this continuation. The engine/CLI explicitly registers the bounded Boolean source frontend. <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/41">PR #41</a> subsequently landed at <code>b1a0298</code> with all 19 CI contexts successful. It adds installed MoonBit source lowering to Ion and independent Boolean truth-table comparison through original source, Scheme and generated execution across required targets in debug/release. The fresh <code>DamianReeves/workbench-invocation-admission</code> continuation starts from merged main <code>40587e6</code> and includes both frontend phases. The local Workbench still compiles Scheme, so exposing MoonBit source selection in the browser/Proton worker remains a separate follow-up. No new connected capabilities are advertised.</p><p id="merge-status">Combined local verification passes. Parent PR #1033 merged at <code>95c1aecb</code> after all 17 final-head contexts completed successfully, skipped or neutral. MoonBit PR #42 merged at <code>40587e6</code> after all 20 final-head contexts passed on <code>7e3fd35</code>. No unresolved review threads remained. The approved admin bypass was used for the parent required-review rule; MoonBit merged normally. Both PR watchers observed MERGED and stopped.</p></section><p>Full architecture, protocol inventory, Mermaid/SVG diagrams and implementation screenshots remain in <a href="morphir-workbench.html">the local workbench HTML design, Revision 30</a>. Live Rust v1 acceptance is complete and merged in PR #36 in morphir-ukvn.5.20. Normative upstream profile publication remains morphir-etg2; evaluation, jobs and cancellation extensions still require upstream adoption.</p><section class="section" id="argparse-portability"><h2>CLI argparse portability check</h2><p>Main <code>1f8c9ad</code> adds the shared-worktree beads database check and requires new or changed task automation to use portable MoonBit scripts. It is incorporated into this continuation at merge <code>775f704</code>; <code>mise run beads:check</code> passes. The existing browser/desktop UI is unaffected.</p><p>A local CLI experiment, preserved in <code>.dev/argparse-spike.patch</code>, replaced handwritten argument loops with <code>moonbitlang/core/argparse</code> command definitions. Contextual help, global output flags, declared repeated values, duplicate/arity checks and the opaque child-argument segment are covered. Five focused parser tests pass per JavaScript, native, Wasm and Wasm GC. Native/JS workspace flows, the installed npm package and real execute/verify through native/Node/npm hosts pass on JS, Wasm GC and native execution targets.</p><p>The actual standalone WASI artifact fails the existing import gate. Core <code>Command::parse</code> retains its optional default-argv branch, which links <code>__moonbit_fs_unstable</code> argument and external-string imports even when the application supplies argv explicitly. The WASI contract currently permits only <code>wasi_snapshot_preview1</code> imports. Unit tests under MoonBit runtime do not establish WASI embedding compatibility.</p><p>That core-argparse experiment was restored after failing the standalone WASI import gate. The adopted Yoorkin/ArgParser integration, documented below, preserves the existing WASI-only contract and now passes full CLI acceptance. Future core-argparse adoption still requires a pure explicit-argv API that passes the same gate. Keep JSON/JSON-lines help and error envelopes, exact values, pipeline last-value overrides and child <code>--help</code>/<code>--json</code>/empty/Unicode arguments in either implementation. The <a href="https://docs.moonbitlang.com/en/stable/tutorial/cli-quickstart.html">official argparse quickstart</a> demonstrates explicit argv for native CLIs; the artifact-level portability finding comes from local builds.</p><h3>Alternative parser comparison</h3><p>Target support is the acceptance requirement. Candidate probes use the repository-pinned MoonBit toolchain and explicit argv. Yoorkin/ArgParser has now passed the full CLI integration described below; other candidates retain only their stated probe evidence.</p><div class="table-wrap"><table><thead><tr><th>Published candidate</th><th>Local evidence and fit</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/moonbit-community/ArgParser">Yoorkin/ArgParser 0.2.1</a></td><td>Adopted after full four-target CLI acceptance. Explicit argv and callback-based option specifications; no argument acquisition or process exit. Small parsing probe checks, tests and release builds pass on native, JS, Wasm and Wasm GC. Its Wasm executable imports only wasi_snapshot_preview1.fd_write and runs under standard WASI. The Morphir wrapper preserves subcommand dispatch, duplicate/required policies, opaque child-argument boundaries and structured help/error envelopes. Full CLI and installed npm acceptance now pass.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/cauchyQ/moonbit-argkit">cauchyQ/moonbit-argkit 0.1.0</a></td><td>Explicit argv and no external dependency. The same four-target small probe and standalone WASI import/run check pass. Published API includes option/schema/command helpers, but it is newer and describes its purpose as examples, teaching projects and small CLI tools. Full Morphir semantics remain untested.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/moonbit-community/cmd/tree/main/core/cli">cli/core/cli 0.2.0</a></td><td>Pure explicit-argv parser with declared repeatable options, duplicate errors, ordered occurrences and last-value helpers. Native/Wasm probes pass and its Wasm executable imports only standard WASI. Published supported_targets excludes JS and Wasm GC, so it is not a direct replacement for all current targets. Broader support requires an upstream package change and acceptance.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/TheWaWaR/clap.mbt">TheWaWaR/clap 0.2.6</a></td><td>Rich subcommands, globals and generated help; explicit argv and injected environment maps. The published package fails compilation against the pinned toolchain because it references removed core strconv APIs, including parse_int64 and StrConvError. Do not adopt it without maintenance and four-target acceptance.</td></tr><tr><td><a href="https://github.com/mizchi/admiral">mizchi/admiral</a></td><td>Wraps core argparse, so it does not by itself resolve the observed default-argv import issue. No compatibility acceptance claimed.</td></tr></tbody></table></div><p>morphir-ukvn.5.19 is complete and merged in PR #36 using Yoorkin/ArgParser and the Morphir schema wrapper. Full acceptance preserves argument strings, forwarding after --, structured envelopes and existing targets. A future upstream pure explicit-argv core argparse API can be reconsidered only after the same artifact-level compatibility checks.</p></section><section class="section" id="live-rust-host"><h2>Live Rust v1 host acceptance</h2><p>The connected browser/proxy slice was first committed at <code>58e54d3</code>, completing <code>morphir-ukvn.5.20</code>. Acceptance uses finos/morphir <code>5c5307d89f34d876e8f1ebf561ec55efbadf9fa0</code>, its pinned morphir-rust submodule <code>04ababf1dbeff10333bdaa70613562157843125a</code>, Rust 1.98.1 and Chromium. An isolated checkout was used because the existing local ecosystem submodule pointers differed from the parent pin. The build and host fixtures were removed after acceptance; the optional local binary is retained in <code>.dev/tools/morphir-rust-5c5307d8</code>.</p><p>The real host exposed a wire-shape mismatch: <code>morphir.workspace.open</code> returns <code>{ snapshot: { projects: [...] } }</code>. The connected adapter now validates that envelope and loads the advertised projects. Invalid snapshots report a diagnostic while compiler capabilities remain available. The v1 fixture now matches the actual response.</p><p>Run <code>mise run test:workbench-live-host -- --host-bin /absolute/path/to/morphir</code>. The portable MoonBit launcher uses core argparse in the standard script runtime. Playwright owns a temporary workspace, private Morphir Home, proxy and host process. Acceptance covers unauthenticated rejection, single-use launch exchange, HttpOnly session authentication, protocol initialization, catalog negotiation, real Gleam compilation, one generated Gleam artifact and project-model opening in Explorer. It waits for the project-model RPC and completed UI update before selecting declarations. A missing binary fails promptly.</p><p>The normal Workbench suite passes 29 focused JavaScript tests, 18 transport/proxy checks and full Chromium workflows. Live acceptance passes twice after correcting its asynchronous model-opening wait. Repository lint, formatting and validation pass. This evidence covers the built-in native Gleam provider. Connected evaluation and cancellation remain unavailable in v1; acceptance sends no invented RPC methods. Upstream profile publication, other provider acceptance, workspace watching, durable daemon recovery and Proton native service IPC remain pending.</p></section><section class="section" id="cli-parser-adoption"><h2>Portable CLI parser adoption</h2><p>The CLI now uses pinned <code>Yoorkin/ArgParser 0.2.1</code> with a Morphir-owned command schema. The library matches flags and consumes option values from explicit argv. The wrapper selects nested commands, checks which options belong to each command, applies repeated/single-option policy, generates contextual help, preserves structured output and keeps child-process arguments opaque after <code>--</code>. Host and engine code still validate execution semantics. New or changed task automation continues to follow main <code>1f8c9ad</code> portable MoonBit script guidance.</p><p>The library's automatic help handler raises immediately. The wrapper uses a private alias for the help flag so the full Morphir argument segment is validated and help/errors stay inside the established human, JSON or JSON-lines envelope. Direct user input of that alias is rejected; it never appears in generated help. Forwarded child arguments remain unchanged, including help/output flags, empty strings, Unicode and additional separators. Inline <code>--name=value</code> is normalized before library parsing without converting scalar values.</p><p>Validation uses MoonBit <code>0.10.14+7d59c7ec9</code>. Seven focused parser tests pass on native, JS, Wasm and Wasm GC. Full CLI workspace integration passes on all four release artifacts and an installed npm package. The actual standalone Wasm executable imports 16 functions, all from <code>wasi_snapshot_preview1</code>, and passes the existing import gate and host runner. No target was removed and no host bindings were added.</p><p>Scalar execution/verify acceptance passes through native, Node and installed npm hosts on generated JS, Wasm GC and native targets. Rich pricing parity passes 32 calls per selected target in debug/release, preserving exact numbers, Float64 bits, UTF-16, Ion extensions, model errors and telemetry isolation. The optional LLVM lane was not selected in this run. It retains its existing explicit toolchain-pin path. Repository lint, formatting, validation and HTML checks pass. Commit <code>bc1127c</code> completes <code>morphir-ukvn.5.19</code> locally; PR #36 merged this continuation at fd4026e.</p></section><section class="section" id="lifecycle-merge"><h2>Lifecycle merge reconciliation</h2><p>PR #34 landed on main at <code>9ce5127</code>. E2 Task 4 is now complete. Merge <code>258471c</code> incorporates its required call statuses, primary/cleanup causes, verification publication and process supervision into this continuation. The CLI schema retains the new <code>--cancel-file</code> option, rejects it outside execution commands and keeps duplicate/arity validation. Eight focused parser tests now cover the merged shape.</p><p>Existing native/Node lifecycle acceptance covers 60 faults and four overlapping contexts. CI includes Linux, macOS and Windows process supervision. These guarantees belong to the host/engine and must be reused by future UI execution adapters. The connected v1 UI still cannot evaluate, cancel server jobs or publish verification output.</p><p>PR #36 merged the Workbench and parser continuations at fd4026e. The next phase is the upstream workbench profile contribution tracked by morphir-etg2, beginning with exact typed value schemas and language-neutral examples from the shipped invocation/outcome codecs. Draft extensions remain unavailable until upstream adoption and capability negotiation.</p></section><section class="section" id="conformance-merge"><h2>Independent conformance merge reconciliation</h2><p>PR #35 landed at <code>4ede1e5</code> while PR #36 checks ran. Merge <code>dd85ebe</code> retains its independent typed expectations, live Scheme and explicitly pinned Rust evaluator lanes, loss-aware telemetry projection and receipts. The <code>conform</code> command uses the portable parser with cases/evaluator/receipt options and cancellation. Nine parser tests pass per target. E2 Task 5 is complete; Task 6 remains pending.</p><p>PR #36 merged at fd4026e with all 16 checks green and both verified review threads resolved. The first upstream profile slice is prepared in an isolated finos/morphir worktree at <code>90f7df0a</code>. Draft typed value schemas and 62 structural fixtures pass the existing JSON Schema CLI. Full semantic MCK fixtures, Ion/JSON roundtrip goldens, host/client adoption and upstream review remain pending.</p></section><section class="section" id="pr36-merge"><h2>PR #36 merge and next phase</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/36">PR #36</a> merged at <code>fd4026eff313ed0d94f7e9ccb3ec79a63864f1e0</code> after all 16 checks passed on reconciled head <code>dd85ebe</code>. Full <code>mise run check</code>, required lint/format/validation and explicit conformance pass. Nine parser tests pass on native, JS, Wasm and Wasm GC. The review fix keeps negotiated host IR aligned with export after local migration; the live-host task is documented. Conformance has 23 independent and Scheme matches per JS/Wasm GC/native debug/release lane. The optional Rust lane was not selected in this continuation.</p><p>The next phase has a local upstream draft commit <code>f8a373ca</code> in <code>/Users/damian/code/github/finos/morphir-workbench-profile</code>, branch <code>DamianReeves/workbench-profile</code>, based on finos/morphir <code>90f7df0a</code>. <code>spec/workbench</code> contains three draft schemas, codec examples, source/admission rules and 62 positive/negative structural fixtures. <code>mise run workbench:schema-check</code> passes formatting, lint, metaschemas and fixtures through the existing JSON Schema CLI. The schemas use draft namespace <code>0.1.0-draft.1</code> and preserve frozen codec IDs and connected protocol v1. This draft is committed locally; upstream publication/review, Ion/JSON roundtrip goldens, semantic MCK adapters and negotiated host/UI adoption remain pending under morphir-etg2.</p></section><section class="section" id="workbench-mck"><h2>Workbench codec qualification</h2><p>Revision 30 records the next upstream slice under <code>morphir-etg2.2</code>. The existing shared Rust <code>morphir mck</code> runner now has an explicit Workbench corpus and adapter command. Parent-owned goldens contain 64 accepted/rejected JSON and Ion text inputs; expectations and case IDs never reach the adapter. Nine draft schemas and 86 structural checks cover value and MCK boundaries, with corpus validation in CI.</p><p>The MoonBit adapter calls the shipped execution value codec. Node and native debug/release lanes each qualify all 64 cases and pass independent report rechecking. Seven pure protocol tests pass JS, native, Wasm and Wasm GC. Parent tests cover malformed claims/observations, wrong results, forged reports, changed golden bytes, bounded evidence and shutdown failures. Scalar payloads preserve exact Int/Decimal, Float64 bits and UTF-16. Decimal admission normalizes for precision checks while codec projection retains coefficient and scale.</p><p>Qualification covers the listed decode projections. Connected protocol v1 is unchanged. Public-entry manifest and invocation/output admission, SDK comparison, Ion binary/reverse-encode goldens, job/lifecycle transport, Rust/TypeScript adapters and upstream host/UI adoption remain pending. E2 Tasks 1–6 are now merged in MoonBit main. Source commits and publication status are recorded in the shared tracker; upstream merge requires maintainer approval.</p></section><section class="section" id="pr37-merge"><h2>PR #37 merge reconciliation</h2><p>MoonBit main advanced to <code>79d4d05e0fdae00b8dc9a29feee3dd898dcf6694</code>. PR #37 merged the installed CLI lifecycle and native telemetry gate after all 20 checks passed on <code>94373ab</code>. All six E2 task beads and their execution plan are closed. The Workbench adapter is rebased onto that merged baseline at <code>d81eeaf</code>; the parent schema/MCK contribution is committed at <code>f8a373ca..81812e4b</code> on finos/morphir base <code>90f7df0a</code>.</p><p>Merged acceptance covers installed JSON/Ion text/binary model input and debug/release JS, Wasm GC and native C lanes on Linux/macOS, plus the required separately pinned LLVM lane on darwin arm64. Native telemetry explicitly enables OTLP HTTP/JSON for correlated spans, logs and metrics with bounded delivery. Unsupported gRPC and compression are not claimed. E2 completion applies to finos/morphir-moonbit; upstream profile adoption, connected jobs, browser generated execution, native IPC and release packaging remain separate.</p></section><section class="section" id="workbench-publication"><h2>Profile contribution landed</h2><p><a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir/pull/1031">finos/morphir PR #1031</a> merged at <code>34b1a8fad805b81e5bab114ec3cfcf500dfc0c68</code>. <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/39">MoonBit PR #39</a> merged at <code>f0cc00465492faa21a834fc9cf3b840283f610a7</code>. Required upstream CI gates and all 20 MoonBit checks passed on the exact reviewed heads. There were no unresolved review threads. The maintainer authorized both merges; GitHub's required-review rule required the administrator merge option for the upstream PR.</p><p>Both local continuation branches now start from the merged main trees. Background PR watchers observed MERGED and exited. The schemas and codec qualification are published upstream; the connected host still advertises protocol v1. Binary/reverse encoding, public-entry manifest and invocation/output admission, SDK comparison, daemon jobs and independent host/UI adoption remain pending under <code>morphir-etg2</code>.</p></section><section class="section" id="back-navigation"><h2>Back navigation</h2><p>The shared top bar has an icon-only rounded arrow button with a Back tooltip and accessible label, visible at mobile widths and with the sidebar collapsed. Declaration selection, reference links, experience switches and worksheet layout changes record destinations. Back restores the earlier selection, search and details/IR view without undoing source edits or changing sidebar collapse choices. Repeated selection adds no history. The latest 100 destinations stay in memory for this session.</p><p>A replacement model clears declaration and search destinations from history and coalesces duplicates, while preserving experience navigation. Returning to a different function uses the existing selection behavior: reset evaluation inputs and results and retain late-reply guards. Browser URL history and evaluation-draft restoration across different definitions remain separate follow-ups.</p><p>Tracked by <code>morphir-etg2.3</code>. Browser acceptance covers keyboard Back, references, no-op selections, search restoration, collapsed sidebar, edited sources, replacement models and mobile visibility. Connected-mode navigation sends no extra RPCs. Packaged Proton 0.3.4 acceptance verifies the same Back button and reference/experience navigation on macOS Apple Silicon. Commit <code>b73660c</code> completes the implementation locally. <code>mise run check</code>, required lint/format/validation and HTML checks pass. Styling commit <code>569afef</code> removes the text and border, uses an original rounded SVG arrow and a circular hover/focus target. Browser acceptance, the local SVG, tooltip and accessible label pass verification. Merge remains pending.</p></section><section class="section" id="declared-admission"><h2>Declared-value admission qualification</h2><p>Merged parent PR #1033 at <code>95c1aecb</code> and MoonBit PR #42 at <code>40587e6</code> publish exact test contract <code>0.1.0-draft.2</code>. The explicit parent-owned kit contains 162 independently fixed cases: 64 retained decode inputs and 98 declared-admission cases. Original draft.1 schemas, tests, 64-case corpus and contract README are byte-identical; its negotiation and reports remain supported.</p><p>The new <code>validate-value</code> operation accepts a JSON or Ion text value together with JSON type descriptors and constructor definitions. The adapter admits a bounded closed declaration graph, rejects duplicates, unresolved names and dormant function types, permits named recursion, then calls the shipped value codec and <code>validate_as</code>. Successful observations retain exact Int/Decimal, Float64 bits and UTF-16. SDK model errors cannot be arguments; ordinary <code>Result.Err</code> values can.</p><svg viewBox="0 0 1040 150" role="img" aria-labelledby="admission-title admission-desc" style="display:block;width:100%;height:auto"><title id="admission-title">Declared-value admission boundary</title><desc id="admission-desc">Independent parent inputs enter the bounded MoonBit declaration guard, then existing codec and type validation. The parent alone compares observations to independent expected results.</desc><g font-family="system-ui,sans-serif" font-size="14" text-anchor="middle"><g fill="#e5f5fc" stroke="#00729e"><rect x="5" y="25" width="230" height="90" rx="10"/><rect x="270" y="25" width="230" height="90" rx="10"/><rect x="535" y="25" width="230" height="90" rx="10"/><rect x="800" y="25" width="230" height="90" rx="10"/></g><g fill="#1c1e21"><text x="120" y="58">Parent-owned input</text><text x="120" y="84">value + type + registry</text><text x="385" y="58">Bounded declarations</text><text x="385" y="84">shape + reference closure</text><text x="650" y="58">Shipped MoonBit boundary</text><text x="650" y="84">codec + validate_as</text><text x="915" y="58">Parent MCK verdict</text><text x="915" y="84">independent fixed goldens</text></g><g fill="#00729e"><path d="M240 65h22v-5l8 10-8 10v-5h-22z"/><path d="M505 65h22v-5l8 10-8 10v-5h-22z"/><path d="M770 65h22v-5l8 10-8 10v-5h-22z"/></g></g></svg><p>Both Node/native debug/release lanes qualify all 162 cases and independently recheck every report. The final runner also requalifies all 64 draft.1 cases in those lanes. Fifteen pure protocol tests pass JS, native, Wasm and Wasm GC. Parent verification covers 27 Workbench Rust tests, four CLI subprocess tests, 133 structural schema tests and both corpus documents; Clippy with denied warnings and formatting pass. Full MoonBit <code>mise run check</code> and required lint/format/validation pass. Type-identity and escaped-Ion budget regressions were reproduced failing before correction.</p><p>The runner selects exact version/operation from the corpus and records it in evidence, rejects cross-draft capabilities and missing/null/altered operation inventories, and recomputes verdicts against the corpus digest. Parent expectations and case IDs never reach the adapter. Large boundary fixtures use compact JSON to keep the review readable; input tokens and fixed expectations are preserved.</p><p>Published and squash-merged through <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir/pull/1033">finos/morphir PR #1033</a> at <code>95c1aecb</code> and <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/42">MoonBit PR #42</a> at <code>40587e6</code>. Remaining work includes public-entry manifests and invocation arity, output admission, SDK comparison, Ion binary/reverse encoding, independent Rust/TypeScript adapters and connected jobs/evaluation. Connected protocol v1 and the browser/Proton runtime behavior remain unchanged by this test contract. Tracked by <code>morphir-etg2.4</code>.</p></section><section class="section" id="invocation-admission"><h2>Public-entry and invocation admission</h2><p>Implemented and independently qualified in <code>morphir-etg2.5</code>: exact offline draft.3 <code>validate-invocations</code>, supplied public-entry allowlist, whole-manifest declaration closure, shipped suite decoding and shared membership/arity/type validation. Parent schemas, independent goldens and operation-aware report checks remain authoritative. See <a href="workbench-invocation-admission.html">the implementation design, evidence and completion checklist</a>. Output values, execution, SDK comparison and connected extensions remain later work.</p><p>The 242-case corpus and saved reports qualify on Node/native debug/release. All 64 draft.1 and 162 draft.2 cases also replay successfully through the final runner; earlier contract artifacts remain byte-identical. Twenty-three pure adapter tests pass JS/native/Wasm/Wasm GC. Parent checks pass 33 focused Rust tests, five CLI subprocess tests, 176 structural schema tests, three corpus documents, denied-warning Clippy and formatting. Independent semantic review found no defect and rejected forged report changes.</p><p>Parent draft PR <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir/pull/1035">#1035</a> is published at <code>1497292e</code>. MoonBit full <code>mise run check</code> and required validation pass; implementation is committed at <code>30e9974</code>. Paired adapter draft PR <a href="https://github.com/finos/morphir-moonbit/pull/44">#44</a> is published. Background CI/review monitors run for both PRs; shared bead <code>morphir-etg2.5</code> records completion. Merge is pending.</p></section><section class="section" id="next-slices"><h2>Next slices and reachability follow-ups</h2><p>Planning update, 04 October 2026. Stage 03 remains upstream profile contribution. Current paired draft PRs #1035/#44 have all 17/20 head check contexts completed successfully or with expected neutral/skipped status, no unresolved threads and no review findings. Their implementation is complete; review and merge remain pending.</p><ol><li>Complete review and land invocation-admission PRs #1035/#44 under maintainer approval.</li><li>Qualify output/outcome admission as the next contract slice: compare successful returned values with declared output types and constructor registries, distinguish model/domain outcomes from ordinary Result.Err and malformed results, and retain primary/cleanup failure semantics.</li><li>Add independent SDK semantic comparison, Ion binary/reverse-encoding coverage and independently qualified Rust/TypeScript adapters as separate slices.</li><li>Complete job/lifecycle/outcome contracts and negotiated host/UI adoption, then native Proton IPC and verified generated-code browser execution. Preserve connected v1 compatibility while extensions are unavailable.</li></ol><p><code>morphir-etg2.6</code> plans explicit permissive admission. Unused declarations and untaken unsupported branches should not block an otherwise supported selected call. Specify deferred checks separately from mandatory selected-entry authorization, request integrity and resource limits; unsupported code fails if reached. Current strict draft.3 remains frozen. Runtime behavior needs its own independent qualification.</p><p><code>morphir-ukvn.6</code> plans tree-shaking separately in the ecosystem roadmap. Compute conservative dependency reachability from explicit entry/export roots, retain required value/type/constructor/SDK and recursive dependencies, preserve metadata and prove retained-entry semantics. Static pruning can share reachability analysis with permissive admission; it cannot by itself determine every untaken runtime branch. These follow-ups do not block the output-admission slice.</p><p>The next visible UI adoption slice is <code>morphir-ukvn.5.23</code>: replace the local hard-coded Scheme catalog/dispatch with supported compiler and generation selections. The portable <code>moonbit-model-bool-v1</code> frontend and MoonBit multi-artifact library generator are ready for browser/Proton integration. Connected dropdowns already use the host catalog, with real Gleam acceptance. Preserve per-language drafts, examples, highlighting and IR metadata. Generation backends and generated execution targets are separate capabilities; browser generated execution and Proton native/provider IPC remain later work. This UI slice can proceed before output-admission contract expansion.</p></section></main></html>

